# Privacy Policy

Last updated: 2026-08-21

DroidOS respects your privacy and is designed to keep user data separated and secure.

## Information we collect
We may collect and store the following information when you use the app:

- Google account information needed to sign in
- YouTube account access needed to read or post live chat messages
- user profile and configuration data
- custom commands, bot settings, stream settings, and saved preferences
- AI usage data needed to personalize bot behavior
- OBS connection configuration if enabled by the user

## How we use your information
We use your information to:

- create and manage your account
- connect your YouTube live chat and stream data
- allow your bot settings and commands to work for your account
- personalize AI responses and bot behavior
- maintain your saved preferences across devices

## Data separation
Each user account is stored separately and is not shared across other users. Your personal data, settings, custom commands, and stream configuration are kept under your account and are not exposed to other accounts.

## Third-party services
DroidOS may use:

- Firebase for authentication and database storage
- Google YouTube APIs for live chat and stream access
- Google AI services for AI reply generation
- OBS WebSocket if enabled for stream overlays and alerts

These services are governed by their respective privacy policies.

## Your choices
You may:

- sign out of your account at any time
- disconnect Google/YouTube access from the app
- remove or update custom content stored in your account

## Data retention
We keep account and configuration data as long as the account remains active. If you delete or remove access, account data may be removed or deactivated in accordance with the app’s account management features.

## Security
We use standard security practices for account authentication and data handling, but no system is fully immune to risk. We recommend keeping your Google account secure and using strong account credentials.

